From d6ffa7985baf62f3cc969ec0fbffcbf7c5ec7c2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TennisConnect Dev <dev@tennisconnect.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 05:52:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add TikTok + Threads social icons to footer and
 maintenance page

lucide-react doesn't ship brand logomarks (TikTok, Threads aren't in
its generic icon set), so added two small standalone SVG components
under client/src/components/icons/ - hand-drawn approximations, since
this sandbox has no SVG rasterizer/browser available to preview them
visually. Flag if they don't look right and I'll adjust the paths.

Both new icons link to the platform's homepage (tiktok.com,
threads.net) as a placeholder, same pattern the existing Facebook/
Instagram links already use (facebook.com, instagram.com rather than
an actual account) - swap in real profile URLs once those accounts
exist.

Added in both places asked: main site footer.tsx (w-8 h-8, next to
Facebook/Instagram) and the /maintenance placeholder page (h-4 w-4,
matching its existing smaller icon size).
